cprog fall2023 eoce 0x0
========================
======Project: Presentation of Concepts======

=====Objective=====
Take something  you've done this semester,  ensure it is in  full working
order, and implement  some means of enabling (via some  unused button, or
some code-based toggle),  to act as a toggle to  display some key concept
and programming-related information to the screen for the user to see, or
give them a choice in how to proceed, potentially impacting game logic.

=====Task=====
Occasionally, there are outreach opportunities  to present the program to
the wider public (Open Houses, Student Expos, High School visits).

As you may  well know, trying to describe to  others, who aren't familiar
with Computer  Science, what  sort s  of things you  do in  your Computer
Science classes, can be  a challenge. So much of what  we do is involving
abstraction, well within the conceptual  domain. We implement things, but
those  things are  merely harboring  various concepts  and patterns,  the
focus of our study.

What I'd  like for you to  do is to enhance  something so that it  can be
used as a demo at such an event, where people could walk up, have minimal
instructions  to operate,  and play  the thing,  while at  certain points
being presented with opportunities to encounter and hopefully think about
some concept embedded therein.

Polished and presentable to the user: imagine this being the sort of demo
you, before starting on your Computer Science journeys here at CCC, would
have appreciated  encountering giving  you some  insight into  the layers
beneath the surface.

Be sure to provide,  either as a comment block in the  source code, or as
an obvious accompanying  file, a summary of what you  did, how to operate
it (assuming  these aren't in  the form of on-screen  instructions during
game play),  what isn't  working, what  from these  specifications hasn't
been achieved.

Your end result will be assessed based on implementation and  correctness
of functionality, along with clear, ease of use operation of the program.

The usual attributes of staying within the spirit of the project, a clean
build, good indentation, descriptive comments, etc. all still apply.

Please provide ALL assets and helper files, along with your source  code,
in order to build your cartridge.
